The Metropolitan Museum of Art — Open Access
  data/cache/met/objects/*.json, data/cache/met/images/*.jpg

  Object metadata from the Met Collection API, released under CC0 1.0. Images
  are cached only for objects the API flags `isPublicDomain`; object 481994 is
  cached as metadata only, with no image.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Lewis and Clark journals — not redistributed here

  The journal text is loaded at ingestion time and is not checked in; the
  captured example boards under `data/examples/` quote extracts from it. Its
  sources are Project Gutenberg ebook 8419 and the Internet Archive item
  `gasssjournalofle00gass` (Gass, ed. Hosmer, A. C. McClurg & Co., 1904,
  reported NOT_IN_COPYRIGHT). Both are public domain in the United States.
  `docs/hackathon-build/corpus-sources.md` records the edition decisions.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Library of Congress, Smithsonian, National Park Service — not redistributed here

  Archive references store catalogue metadata, a rights statement copied
  verbatim from the repository, and a link. Item files are cached outside
  version control (`data/archive-cache/`, git-ignored). Per ADR-024 no reference
  reaches `trusted` without a person accepting its provenance; the model never
  decides rights.
